/-!
# The residue-field dictionary at a place: vocabulary

This file sets up the two notions of the chapter that are used by more than one of its files:

* `cyclotomicClosure p` — the compositum of the `K⟮ζ⟯` inside `K'` over all primitive `n`-th roots
  of unity with `p ∤ n`: the global analogue of `κ(μ_{p'}) = κ^ur`, the maximal unramified
  extension of the local field `κ = K_𝔭` (whose residue characteristic is `p`).
* `ResidueCardMatches A q` — the **residue-cardinality normalisation**: `q` is the cardinality of
  the residue field of the prime of `K` below the place `A`.  This is a genuine hypothesis in
  `NK.ResidueFrob.placeLevelBridgeCore_of_inputs` (the `q` of `NK.FrobeniusBridge.PlaceLevelData`
  is not *a priori* the residue cardinality of the base prime: it is pinned down by
  `NK.LocalTame.TameData` only through the torsion of the tame abelianisation); it is discharged
  in `Submission/Work/ResidueFrob/LocalStructureInputs.lean`, where `q` is *defined* as the
  residue cardinality of the completion.

## A remark on the inertia half, for readers of the classical proof

The third field of `NK.FrobeniusBridge.PlaceLevelBridgeCore` is the statement that the level
inertia subgroups of the tower below `A` are the images of the local inertia subgroup.  One might
try to reduce it to the following "cyclotomic" statement:

  *the cyclotomic form*: every `g` acting trivially on the residue field of the finite normal level
  `L` at the prime below `A` fixes the elements of `L ∩ K(μ_{p'})` (i.e. the elements of `L` lying
  in `cyclotomicClosure p`).

That statement is *not* the right one to reduce to, for a reason that is worth recording: the
subfield `L ⊓ K(μ_{p'})` of `L` is only the part of the maximal unramified-at-`𝔭` subextension of
`L` that is generated by roots of unity.  For example, with `K = ℚ`, `p = 3` and `L` the Galois
closure of `x³ - x - 1` (discriminant `-23`, so `3` is unramified in `L`), `L` is unramified at
`3` without being contained in `ℚ(μ_{3'})`; the level inertia is trivial there, so the statement is
true there but carries no information about the rest of the unramified part.  The correct
statement is the one used here: the level inertia is, modulo the fixing subgroup of the level, the
*local* inertia `I_κ = Gal(κ̄/κ(μ_{p'}))` — which is precisely what
`NK.ResidueFrob.LevelInertiaCovered` says, and which is *proved* in this chapter
(`NK.ResidueFrob.levelInertiaCovered_of_tameData`) rather than assumed.
-/

namespace NK.ResidueFrob

open scoped Pointwise Classical
open IntermediateField

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

variable {K : Type*} [Field K] [NumberField K]
variable {K' : Type*} [Field K'] [Algebra K K'] [IsSepClosure K K']

/-- **The cyclotomic closure of `K` in `K'` away from `p`**: the compositum of the simple
extensions `K⟮ζ⟯` over all primitive `n`-th roots of unity `ζ` with `p ∤ n`.

Over the local field `κ = K_𝔭` (so `p` the residue characteristic) this is `κ(μ_{p'})`, the maximal
unramified extension of `κ`. -/
noncomputable def cyclotomicClosure (p : ℕ) : IntermediateField K K' :=
  ⨆ (n : {n : ℕ // ¬ p ∣ n}) (ζ : K') (_ : IsPrimitiveRoot ζ (n : ℕ)), K⟮ζ⟯

/-- A primitive `n`-th root of unity with `p ∤ n` lies in the cyclotomic closure. -/
theorem mem_cyclotomicClosure {p n : ℕ} (hn : ¬ p ∣ n) {ζ : K'} (hζ : IsPrimitiveRoot ζ n) :
    ζ ∈ cyclotomicClosure (K := K) (K' := K') p :=
  (le_iSup (fun n : {n : ℕ // ¬ p ∣ n} =>
      ⨆ (ζ : K') (_ : IsPrimitiveRoot ζ (n : ℕ)), K⟮ζ⟯) ⟨n, hn⟩)
    ((le_iSup (fun ζ : K' => ⨆ (_ : IsPrimitiveRoot ζ n), K⟮ζ⟯) ζ)
      ((le_iSup (fun _ : IsPrimitiveRoot ζ n => K⟮ζ⟯) hζ)
        (IntermediateField.mem_adjoin_simple_self K ζ)))

/-- **The residue cardinality of the place `A`**: `q` is the cardinality of the residue field of
the prime of `K` below `A`.  This is the number by which the Frobenius of the level acts on the
level's residue field, and by which a local Frobenius lift acts on the roots of unity. -/
def ResidueCardMatches (A : NK.FrobeniusBridge.FinitePlaceOf K K') (q : ℕ) : Prop :=
  q = Nat.card (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K ⧸
    (Submission.NeukirchUchida.primeOf A.1 A.2).asIdeal)

end NK.ResidueFrob
